{"id": "EUVD-2026-93140", "enisaUuid": "0257bfb8-ccc5-3902-8ae4-ad3d8d1139d4", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nmmc: hsq: Fix use-after-free in retry work\n\nmmc_hsq_pump_requests() queues retry_work when request_atomic() returns\n-EBUSY; today sdhci-sprd is the only consumer that implements\nrequest_atomic(). The work is embedded in a devm-allocated mmc_hsq, but\nis never cancelled during driver removal. Work still pending at unbind\ncan therefore run after the devm allocation has been released and\ndereference hsq->mmc and hsq->mrq.\n\nUse devm_work_autocancel() to cancel and drain retry_work before the devm\nallocation is released. By the time devres cleanup begins,\nmmc_remove_host() has already stopped the host, so no new requests can\narm the work.\n\nThis issue was found by an in-house static analysis tool.", "datePublished": "2026-10-06T08:44:48", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:15:43", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c50d6515bffb148c2c12be6d587ec201dfab4c34", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/df2eb59fd9eb33663dc1053f5a4ed851e0aa1f67", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8439bf262ce3267bcfee29d3c61605f1731a2271", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/45341b341642c377192c95e4d48e0a859cf85f42", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5d132990475f02cfa1debe03d50b479432864ebd"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98212", "GHSA-9ffv-qr59-hrp8"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "105a820c-7ee4-3d22-bd67-148f137debd0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.158"}, {"id": "2301aeef-66fe-35a3-bdf8-34be9b912ce6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.8"}, {"id": "2993ff7b-afed-3406-bc3b-29c23a15cb2c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6db96e5810e0a6a345b7d78549de7676ae5b2662 <8439bf262ce3267bcfee29d3c61605f1731a2271"}, {"id": "35fcb37e-de27-39ff-bc9f-f7eeb9d671c0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "611c9707-ebe4-3506-bd02-6bb42f2d665c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.54"}, {"id": "8c9792fc-0e25-3248-b407-194f96c938ed", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6db96e5810e0a6a345b7d78549de7676ae5b2662 <5d132990475f02cfa1debe03d50b479432864ebd"}, {"id": "92d7f469-341e-397d-b519-7a3e42d95fa9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "d233b980-004f-30d1-b5cf-ac75bfc2d7f2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.112"}, {"id": "e285128f-b2b4-3133-b25a-c1ff6bcb4df4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6db96e5810e0a6a345b7d78549de7676ae5b2662 <c50d6515bffb148c2c12be6d587ec201dfab4c34"}, {"id": "f57fe592-6e85-357e-b505-146439617d65", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6db96e5810e0a6a345b7d78549de7676ae5b2662 <45341b341642c377192c95e4d48e0a859cf85f42"}, {"id": "f827262a-9ce2-3524-b6e7-de609d485ab8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.8"}, {"id": "ff342c5f-b2f1-39a5-b202-62786dcf6fc4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6db96e5810e0a6a345b7d78549de7676ae5b2662 <df2eb59fd9eb33663dc1053f5a4ed851e0aa1f67"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "6b213e0d-bbfa-3322-ab23-5abd0bef60e0", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}